# Keep the image minimal: only what the container needs gets sent to the build.
# Patterns match from the context root; **/ reaches into subdirectories.
# config/ is NOT ignored: the Dockerfile bakes config/enabled-tools.txt into
# the image (the read-only tool list launch.py enforces).
scripts/
recipes/
# Maintainer-only folders the image never copies: the eval suite and its runs
# (evals/runs/ too), the Grafana dashboards, and ruff's cache.
evals/
dashboards/
.ruff_cache/
# Hypothesis's example cache from local test runs.
**/.hypothesis/
README.md
.git
.gitignore
.env*
tokens/
*.secret
**/*.token
garmin_tokens.json
.garminconnect*
**/*garminconnect_base64*
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.venv/
venv/
**/*.local.md
# Docker Compose files, the tunnel token and the docs: none of them belongs
# in the image (compose.yaml, docs/deploy-docker.md).
compose.yaml
tunnel.env
**/*.env
docs/
SECURITY.md
CHANGELOG.md
# Garmin credentials in their newer forms: the base64 copy garmin-mcp-auth
# writes (GARMINTOKENS_BASE64) and the key-mode token cache folder.
**/*garmin_tokens.base64*
**/garmin-key/
# ext/ is copied whole (COPY ext/ /opt/garmin-ext/), minus its tests and docs.
ext/test_*.py
ext/fixtures/
ext/README.md
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
